Michael Beutjer wrote:

> Does anyone have any benchmarks for comparing old PDP 11's (like a 55,
> or a 94) to modern processors?  I've done a net search and found the
> village.org pages, but there's nothing that gets me to a Vax or
> Pentium, or Sparc, etc.
>
> Thanks!
> Michael Beutjer

Jerome Fine replies:I do not have exact figures.  However, as a rule of
thumb:
PPD 11/23     9 minutes
PDP 11/73     4 1/2 minutes
PDP 11/83     3 minutes
PDP 11/93     about 2.7 minutes or more
Usual test was a large assembly using a virtual memory disk.
Consequently,
there was no disk I/O involved (I just wanted to measure the CPU speed).
The operating system was RT-11.  The 11/94 in this case would be the same
as an 11/93.  The same applies to the 11/84 and the 11/83.  In general,
DEC rates the uVAX II as equal to the PDP 11/73 or the PDP 11/83
or the PDP 11/93 depending on the job mix and available memory.





