Wayne Sewell wrote:
> Does it make sense to store this information in a format that can be read only
> by PCs?  

PDF is a document standard which is available on a great many platforms
and appeared first on MACs (the desktop publishing standard). Any
postscript output
can be converted to PDF format and can be exchanged to any platform with
a reader even if that platform doesn't have the fonts etc etc. It is a
totally self contained document.

For textual stuff, it is perhaps overblown, but for documents where
presentation and format is important or documents which contain
graphics, images etc, PDF makes it easy to download and then view, print
etc.

As a matter of fact, the PDF format now is good enough to be a
documentation standard with links, index, bookmarks etc. Bye bye
bookreader :-( :-( :-(



