Eddie Esqueda <eesqueda@jaws.greatwhite.com> writes:

> I was wondering if there are any significant differences between OpenVMS
> & AlphaVMS. My company is migrating from a VAX 4705, running OpenVMS, to
> an Alpha( model ??) running AlphaVMS.
> 
> Is there going to be a lot for me to "re-learn?" Is the user interface
> similar or different?
> Any other info will help.

There is no such thing as "AlphaVMS". There is "OpenVMS for VAX" and
"OpenVMS for Alpha". These are virtually identical products. There are
internal differences due to the change in page size on the Alpha, but
most users could not tell the difference and both may run in a single
VMScluster (formerly VAXcluster).

Another are of change is device drivers.

If you are doing system level programming, you may need to learn some
new stuff, but otherwise, don't worry.
