with DEC, R.S. cannnot provide any service or parts, most of the time,
they don't know what your talking about anyway. More than likely, the
drive just died and you need to replace it. DO NOT, I repeat DO NOT put
a regular ole floppy in its place, or when you power up, it, the new
drive, will blow you floppy controller. The floppy drive gets its power
from the controller and when you power up the system, the +5 volts from
the new floppy drive will back feed to the floppy controller thru the
data/pwr cable. Call a local broker and tell them what you have and most
of them will have what you need.
Good Luck,
