Y'know, a friend of mine bought a Multia...he had the OSF1 CDROM,
and bought an NEC external SCSI cdrom drive from Fry's (local
electronics store).  We spent a day or two trying to get the
software to install on the box, but kept getting mysterious
SCSI errors trying to get it to load.  Finally, in frustration,
he called DEC tech support.  They were very nice, very
conscientious, and acknowledged that there had occaisonally
been some problems with the firmware recognizing certain
SCSI drives properly.  So, they shipped him a free CD-ROM
drive so that he could get the software installed.  Just
like that.  Very straightforward, no beating around the bush,
no making a fuss because he'd bought it for $325 from
www.onsale.com and not from them.

To me, that's what makes DEC special, and it's why I still
recommend DEC over other vendors--in every case, when I've
dealt with them, they've gone out of their way to make SURE
your system works--at least, when reasonable.  I'm not expecting
anyone from DEC to ride to my rescue regarding the corrupt ADVfs
disk problem I have right now...  :-)

Matt
