Why not count the number of sick people in a doctor's office and use
that as a gauge of the health of the general population?

The number of problems posted to newsgroups related to NT has a lot
more to do with the number of people trying to use the product and the
relative lack of experience those people have with the product, than
the relibility of NT.

It's been a LONG time since VMS was a growth market.  (I know that
because I earn my living doing VMS consulting.)  On the other hand NT
has gone from an installed base of zero 4 years ago to outselling just
about every other server platform.  Given that VMS is a mature product
with a static (or declining) installed base and plenty of experienced
system managers, it only makes sense that VMS newgroups would contain
fewer problem posts.

The only real way to find out how well NT works is to try it.



