This happens to a lot of UDBs. If you've got a PC board cleaning
machine, drop the motherboard it in there. If not, put it in the
diswasher. (Yes, I am serious.) Make darn sure there's no soap in
it, and that the heating element for drying the dishes is off. When
done, rinse the board with distilled water and let it dry. That
often takes enough flux of the board that it starts working again.
Of course, this procedure might also kill it entirely, but in that
case you've not lost much, have you? :-)

