Your new RQDX3 card is probably OK.  The purpose of the DEC FS diagnostic
is to scribble on a normally read-only portion of the disk that contains,
among other things, the information needed to identify the type of drive
to the RQDX3.  If this area is blank (non-DEC disk) or damaged, only
the FS diangostic will make the disk mountable again.

My experience with this is to have formatted numerous disks with the FS
formatter.  What _I_ wish I had was a smallish disk (RD31, for example)
that I could mount and boot with the formatter on it.  Does anyone out
there know how to put the diagnostics on a different media than TK50?


