  That's a Dataproducts B300 printer - the only difference between the LP25
and the B300 is the cover style. It should have a Dataproducts interface
(50-pin D-series connector). There's a pocket in the printer (to the right
of and behind the control panel) which should have an operator's guide with
the most common info in it.

  If you were here in the US I'd recommend Consultex (http://www.consultex-inc.
com) for manuals and parts. The items you can get (in order of increasing
technical info and expense) are:

  Operator's Guide
  Owner's Manual
  Master Support & Logistics Manual
  B-series History File

