Ana Pedraz wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> Has anyone got a clue of how to define a new pci scsi card on an
> Alpha2100 running OSF3.2c kernel?
> 
> What happens is, when you install the cards and power the machine up, if
> do a "show config" or "show devices" from the "promt", you can see the
> two new cards and the devices attached to them.
> The problem comes when you boot the machine, at that time , if you use
> "scu", then you only see bus 0 and bus 1, but nothing about the two new
> cards.
> 

Well, the procedure is (from DEC):

1. power up and stop boot (press Ctrl-C at boot time)
2. issue: boot -file genvmunix (boot with generic kernel)
3. doconfig (this should overwrite configuration file, you might want to
save it first)
4. mv <new kernel> / (consult man doconfig)
5. shutdown now ; halt
6. at firmware prompt issue boot.

Hope that helps. Anyway, it's been a while since I've done that, so
consult doconfig man pages.

Nix.



