I know this is not my field of expertise, but this is what I've
been able to find out ...

1)  The problem you are having is down to the fact that the 100Mhz
    Pentium has an 8k external cache, and the 166Mhz Overdrive chip
    has a 16k external cache.  The cache difference is causing a PCI
    resource conflict during boot up, and it hangs at this point,
    right?
     		180:  Cache configuration

2)  As a (temporary) work around, the 166Mhz Overdrive Chip will
    function if you disable the external cache.  Obviously you'll
    get a performance hit from this, but tests using a freeware app
    called "Wintune" show that only average RAM copy is slightly
    slower than the 100Mhz chip.  All others, Dhrystone (MIPS),
    Whetstones (MFLOPS), Video (MP/s) and Avg. RAM reads, still show
    an increase in performance.  Average RAM writes stay the same.

3)  You are not alone.  Digital is very aware of this problem, as
    some of its employees also have Starion 930's and have tried
    the same thing you have.  And the investigation of this problem
    by Digital Engineering is not (yet) closed. BUT NO PROMISES OK !!

Lastly ... I will keep an eye on this problem internaly, and watch
for future developments.  When there is a conclusion, I will drop you
a mail.  

BUT, I will ONLY do this on one condition.  I am not amused with your
choice of language in your recent articles on this subject.  If I see
any repeat articles of this kind, I will dump your e-mail address in
the bit-bucket, forget you even exist, and leave you out to dry!  I
hope I have made myself quite clear!

John
