> and was found by someone (Percy Spencer) working at a commercial company
> with a military device (a magnetron.) [Panati's, op cite, page 125]
> The magnetron was developed in 1940 (part *of* WWII, not *after* WWII).
> 
> 
> One could argue that military technology has had notable consumer
