>      We have a proprietary machine running VMS that writes data
> to a Pioneer 720 optical disk drive.  We think that the data are
> on the optical disk in VMS filesystem format.  We would like to
> read the optical disk on UNIX (Sun) systems.  Does anyone know
> whether this is possible or know of a program that can read a
> VMS-created optical disk on a UNIX machine?  We've played around
> with various ways to do this, but always end up with bunches of
> zero-length files after attempts at VMS-to-UNIX conversion.
