Write to intraco.com (Bill Tabor, tabor@intraco.com, for example
might be able to comment.) I wrote them a package awhile back
that allows Digital Unix to read VMS disks as filesystems.

In addition there's a package on most any recent sigtapes from
DECUS called ods-2-reader.c or some variant thereof. This is
a utility that will read files or directories off an ods-2 disk.

To run this on a big-endian machine like a Sun will take a little
tweaking; the package runs ok on dunix and is even present in
binary on the tapes. the source file should be someplace on the
www.decus.org site (http and ftp).



