This may sound strange and long overdue, but our venerable Vax 11/780 is dead -
it had been running continuously (more or less of course as it wasn't on a
ups and there were repairs) since June 1984. And the only hardware maintenance
or repair in the last 3 years being the replacement of an RA81!

It was due to be scrapped in December or January when our group makes the move
to our new building. But it died its own way, double cpu error during boot up
(my guess is a WCS parity error).

I won't even try to explain the pathologies and bizarrities of our organization
that allowed me to keep it running that long. Needless to say the utilities
don't come out of our budget. It was on hardware maintenance for the first
several years and software support for a few more. But it merrily lumbered
along running PMDF and CMU-TEK doing some mail service. Our main
rationalization was that it had a bunch of our old modelling and data analysis
code that we were either too lazy or used so seldom to port over to other
boxes.

This must be some record? Are any other 780's still out there running? Or any
that have run that long?

RIP: Vax 11/780, 84096162x:
	delivered 18-Jan-1984, hardware installed 22-Jun-1984, 
	VMS 3.4 installed 16-Jul-1984; 
	died 19-Sep-1997.



