I have NT 4 SP3 on an AlphaServer 400 (and on a couple of Micron
PPROs) and it is pretty reliable. If the system is purely a server and
you aren't installing software then reboots are rare (< monthly). The
AS is running with no local user normally whereas the PPROs are
on desktops, get software installed, and have to be rebooted.

It's still not as solid as VMS. I have one VMS server which has to be
rebooted once a year to update the software licenses, but hardly
ever otherwise.

The issue is more one of availability, which requires dual access
disks and VMS clusters. These are definitely more robust than NT
can achieve at present, but it's coming along fast.

