As you said, it's a limited market.  Do you have any idea what's
involved in getting things qualified for use on aircraft, particularly
commercial aircraft?  I don't, but I've heard that it's tough.

Granted, the VOD system wouldn't be considered in any way critical to
the operation of the aircraft (well, the passengers might think it
is...) but there are many other considerations, such as space, power,
vibration, etc.  DEC couldn't just drop an ordinary Alphaserver into a
767 with ordinary storage, it would have to be a product designed
specifically for that environment.

It's a project better left to the companies with experience doing that
sort of thing.  In any case, it wouldn't have to be an all-DEC system;
if it were "Alpha Powered" DEC could still pay to advertise on it.

