> What is needed to upgrade a DECpc XL 590 from a single to dual Pentium
> configuration?

The last two people to try it from this group report that it doesn't work.
The DECpc XL dual CPU daughterboard has one jumper on it for 60 or 66 mhz
bus speed and doesn't recognize both CPUs. If you have a daughtercard that
has two jumpers, 60/66 and (3/2x)/(2x) then you only need to drop in the
second CPU and it will boot as a dual processor. But as far I know (not a
DEC tech) that daughterboard started with the Celebris XL 590.

