Organization: @Home Network
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Marcel Timmer wrote:
> 
> Does anybody know the jumpersettings for a 500MHz cpu on the LX
> motherboard?
> The manual only mentiones 466, 533 and 600.
> 
> Or is this "Digital marketing"
> 
> TIA
> Marcel
The board does not go to 500Mhz.

There is a master clock that manages the CPU, Cache and Memory buses. 
This is clocked at 66Mhz increments.  Therefore, the only speeds
supported on the PC 164LX is 466, 533, 600. . .officially.  The board
can also go in higher clock speeds, with a minor modification to the
voltage regulation for the processor to 667Mhz, 733Mhz and 800Mhz.



