Allied Telesis makes a line of small (about 2 1/2" long) transceivers which plug
directly into the AUI port. You don't need a transceiver cable.

The AT-210T is the twisted pair version. I think the BNC version is a AT-MX10, but I'm
not positive about the part number.

These are nice little units and can be found for about $25 each. I've had good luck
finding them in Macintosh mail order catalogues.

For AUI ports with limited access, there is a "slim line" version (Add a "S" to then
end of the model number, e.g., AT-210TS). This adds about 1/2" to the transceiver as a
small "snout" to reach the AUI port. I think the 4000/VLC requires this. (Sorry, I
don't have a VLC here to test it with.)

Good luck!

