Put yourself in the shoes of a manager of a truly legacy system such as 
a DG, UNYSYS etc  machine.

Without experience in running a "server/serious" application on NT, and
without experience in running a "serious/server" application on VMS, how
can you expect that manager to be able to quantify the "true"
maintenance costs
of either solutions ?

You can't. So, in the end, the manager takes the hard costs as furnished
by 
the companies and NT comes out way ahead.

(Note that the VMS maintenance costs may include free upgrades while NT
may not (ok, theoretically quantifiable if you know ahead of time how
many upgrades will be available for both in the coming year), and VMS
upgrades may end up costing much less in consultant costs because, being
a mature system,
upgrades are increasingly simpler while NT is still in puberty growing
in 
leaps and bounds that are not as well coordinated. (Remember the upgrade
from VMS 4.7 to 5.0 ?)



