It takes a waveguide "pipe" microns wide to support an optical mode. If
you want to turn a corner, the mode has to be reflected somehow,
introducing loss and mode conversion. Optical logic has not been
developed to the point of usefulness, consequently logical operations
still would have to be done with electrical signals. The required
conversion steps introduce significant delay and require power.

not an attractive picture at this point.

