You can run VAX/VMS or ULTRIX (based on BSD UNIX) from Digital, or
you can - I presume - get a free UNIX variant (FreeBSD, NetBSD, 
LINUX, who knows what).

VMS or ULTRIX is sold by Digital & distributors (though, I don't
know about current ULTRIX availability or pricing for either).

> Q2 How will they work in with my Win95 and NT4 Network.

For VMS you can get PATHWORKS (from Digital); it makes the
VMS system act as a LAN Manager server.

There was also a PATHWORKS release for ULTRIX.

You can also get a free LAN Man/SMB (Server Message Block)
server called SAMBA and use it (at least on the UNIX derivatives).

