Subject: Re: df showing wrong disk usage on an advanced FS
Date: 1997/09/19
Message-ID: <34222A9D.41C6@mantegna.casaccia.enea.it>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 273734564
References: <341E9920.9004C911@ibsgmbh.de> <34218944.5438@EUnet.yu>
Organization: ENEA
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


Probably it depends on a bug of the 

quotacheck -a

occurring when the fsck parameters in the /etc/fstab are > 0

The fsck parameter is the last number on each line of /etc/fstab.

Please note that a quotacheck -a is iusssed
at boot time by 

/sbin/init.d/quota 


There are 2 turnaround of the problem:

1) put to 0 the fsck parameters in /etc/fstab

2) change the quotacheck -a in /sbin/init.d/quota
   into multiple quotacheck (one for each fs to be checked)

Of course if you don't do 1) you have never to use
quoatcheck -a 


Bye bye from Italy
