> "VaxStation II" on them, although I also have a MicroVax II manual in
> there - I'm not really sure though.  How on earth do I tell the
> difference???

The only (well, major, anyway) difference between the MicroVAX II and
the VAXstation II is the presence of a VCB01 or VCB02 graphics
controller.  So, your manuals are mostly accurate.

The CPU goes probing for the VCB on power up.  If it finds one, it uses
it as the console instead of the serial port.

