This agrees with the copy of the manual that we have in the office with
our VRC16s.  _However_, after much searching, I have establised that (as
usual with DEC monitors) there are at least 2 variants, the -CA and -HA.
It is highly likely that the spec above refers to the -CA (although we
bought -HAs), while the -HA will almost certainly run up to 72Hz at the
maximum resolution of 1280x1024.  This accords with the naming convention
used by the VRT models.  I couldn't find anything really definitive anywhere
on Digital's web pages, but there were enough clues to suggest this to be
true.

