I have NEVER seen that.  I have 1 2100 with 15 RZ29-VA's and 1 RZ28-??
installed internally.  It also has 4 CPU's, 3 memory boards and all of 
it's EISA and PCI slots filled.  It is running with no problem.  The thing 
you have to do is buy the second power supply.  Part #H7893-AA.

You have to also make sure that the redundant power jumper(W1) is NOT
on.  Look at your 2100 owner's guide for more details.  I just added 
7 RZ29-VA's to a 2100A yesterday with no problems.  The internal shelf 
for a 2100 or 2100a (Part # BA35-SA) was only $500 from my digital 
reseller.   Much cheaper than the external shelf.  Check your Owner's 
Guide for configuration options.   In fact I would not do this without
a copy of the owner's guide handy.  

If you ever want to know what is supported on a 2100 go to: 

http://www.digital.com/
info/alphaserver/tech_docs/alphasrv2100/docs/supported_options.html
(How do you format a wide html address for usenet?)

Change the 2100 to your favaorite model and it will be there.  You 
will see that the RZ29's are there in all of their flavors.  

Good luck,

