Don't worry about it. I get the same error on my VS3100 with a ST41200N.

I bet that if you do a SHOW DEVICE you will see that the SCSI INQUIRY data is
truncated.  What I am guessing is happening (If someone knows different,
please enlighten us) is that the INQUIRY data is too long and is tripping
some error. I've been running this disk for years and VMS hasn't had problems
with drive, so I think the error is harmless.

The biggest problem I have with it is that it keeps my machine from
autobooting. <sigh>

BTW: If I move the same drive to a VS4000, I don't get the error, but SHOW
DEVICE still truncates the INQUIRY data.

