> Hey guys/gals, a quick question if you can help me..
> 
> I am looking to put 12 RZ29B-VA's in an Alphaserver 2100 4/233,
> connected, in two internal wide storageworks bays.
> 
> My question is: Is temperature likely to be a problem here ? - I have
> seen no warnings about this from any DEC sources, and indeed one of
> the 'golden egg' examples has a number of internal drives in such a
> configuration. The machine itself is in an air-conditioned vault,
> which is very capable of cooling the room down to 70c and below.
> 
> However, I feel sure that I've seen someone mention the 7200rpm drives
> as not being supported internally... any ideas ??

I'm not entirely sure about 12 RZ29s in a 2100.  The fan immediately
behind the drive bays pulls most of it's air through the opening to the
left of the shelves; not much of that air comes through the shelves. 
There's not much in the way of ventilation holes in the back of the
storage shelves.

Personally, I wounldn't take the chance.  Get a couple of external
towers with fans rated for RZ29s, and be completely safe.

In any case, if you don't have it already, get that secoond power
supply.

