In article <874292843.9653@dejanews.com>, zouy@sundaynet.com writes:
:i have a dec HiNote Ultra CS475.
:
:the password for SETUP was been forgot, so i can't go
:into SETUP by press 'fn'&'F3' , how can i clear it ?

  If you do not remember the firmware password and if you have not created
  a floppy "backup" of the password...

  You will need to send the HiNote system in for service -- there is no way
  around this password in the field -- the firmware password is a "hard"
  protection.  The service requirement is a deliberate design choice, and
  this is explicitly intended to discourage system theft.

  [This behaviour and this requirement is clearly documented in the HiNote
  manuals that I have looked at.]

  Folks that have their HiNote stolen, and have set a firmware password,
  can report the theft -- when the system comes back for service...

