> Surely there is a way to get a HiNote 800x600 to work properly at 640x480
> resolution so that I can connect to a computer overhead projection system
> which requires the lower projection. I've tried looking through the
> drivers on digital's web site - no joy there. If I use quickres to get to
> the lower projection it doesn't use the whole screen - I then have an
> inch of black space around the edge of the window, and the window is
> shrunk horizontally.If I use the higher resolution the top and bottom get
> chopped off.

An LCD panel has a fixed number of pixels. If the panel has
800x600 pixels, and you put up an image at 640x480, then 
some pixels are going to be unused.

That's the black space you see.

Technically, a driver could stretch the image to cover the
whole area, but I'm sure that the results would most often
be less than acceptable; try taking a screendump of a
640x480 display and stretch it to 800x600 in a paint program
to see what I mean).

