>  Although unmentionoed in the INDEX file, there seems to be a copy
>of rt-11v4 at ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/sim/software under the 
>filename rt11swre.tar.Z.  Could it be that someone has released it
>for public consumption?

If you uncompress and untar this file, you'll find the license
that Bob Supnik negotiated with Mentec.  It's a binaries-only license,
and only good for running under *his* emulator.  In other words,
"public consumption", but only under some rather strict conditions.
You'll notice that the license also allows users of Bob's emulator
to run some older versions of RSX-11M, 11M+, and RSTS/E.  One can only
hope that images of these OS's will become ftp'able in the future :-)

In appreciation of Bob's efforts so far, and in hope that he'll be
able to negotiate similar licenses in the future with other
copyright holders, I think it'd be best if the terms of the license were not
abused!

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



