Yiorgos Alexandris wrote:
> 
> Hello everyone.
>         Does anyone know how I can make a DEC Alpha running OSF1 behave as a
> router (i.e., as a gateway doing IP forwarding)? I would appreciate any help.
> Bye,
> 
>                                                         Yiorgos Alexandris

Hello Yiorgos

I,ve running a DEC Alpha (DU 3.2d) as an IP router. 

o To enable routing you have to configure IP forwarding:

  # rcmgr set ROUTER yes
  # rcmgr set ROUTED yes

o To specify anadditional IP address within a different IP net you
should create
  a shell script, which is executed after the network initialization
during the
  boot phase. Name this script "/sbin/rc3.d/S00inet_router". It should
  contain the following line(s):

  ifconfig <nic> alias <additional IP address> netmask <...> broadcast
<...>

  example: IP address within the second network is 192.168.13.1, netmask
is 255.255.255.0,
           network interface is "tu0" (Ethernet)

  ifconfig tu0 alias 192.168.13.1 netmask 255.255.255.0 broadcast
192.168.1.255


This works well with one network interface card.

Regards,

Juergen Luther.
