LSM has mirroring and stripping features. It is software RAID 0 and/or
1. I have Mylex RAID 3-port controller, so, you can imagine that I'm not
interested in sw RAID.

AdvFS has the ability to create "logical" drive - file domain, from
anything that behaves as UNIX raw device; disk partititions, LVM volumes
or LSM volumes. Several file systems - file sets can coexist in a single
domain, sharing the available space.

In my opinion, if you're going to use both LSM and AdvFS, let LSM handle
multi-volume-into-logical-drive mechanism.

I've never tried LSM. How robust is it?

Nix.



