In article <34144c46.5618970@news.mindspring.com>, storie@mindspring.com (Michael Storie) writes:
:I'm looking for information on setting up hardware devices like RAID
:and print etc on a DEC Alpha running VMS.

  With a storage device (disk or tape) that is supported by the version
  of OpenVMS in use, usually little more than connecting the device is
  required.

  OpenVMS -- VAX or Alpha -- will automatically configure a storage device
  that has been set up per the storage device's documentation during the
  OpenVMS bootstrap.  (You may need to power down the OpenVMS host, or the
  storage controller, or both.  And when powering up, normally the storage
  devices should be powered up before the OpenVMS host.  See the storage
  device's documentation.)

  With disks, once configured, you will need to issue an appropriate
  MOUNT command.  This is usually performed by adding explicit DCL
  command(s), such as MOUNT, in SYS$STARTUP:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM.

  Some devices -- such as printers and more complex storage devices
  such as RAID controllers -- can require host configuration.  For
  further information on configuring a print queue, please see the
  OpenVMS System Management manual, available online -- see below.
  There are basic queue examples in the SYS$SYSTEM:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM
  site-specific startup command procedure, as well.

:  Does anyone know where I
:can obtain either online or downloadable system configuration
:information this?

  Parts of the OpenVMS documentation set are available online at
  http://www.openvms.digital.com:81/.

  I would strongly recommend acquiring a local CD-ROM or hardcopy
  of the documentation set.  (You really need this local access.)

  Documentation for specific hardware devices is usually shipped
  with the device.  This documentation will help you correctly
  connect the device, and correctly configure the device settings,
  such as setting the SCSI address on a SCSI storage device...

:I'm sorry that I can't be more specific about
:hardware being used etc.., but I don't have that information in front
:of me.

  As long as you realize that vague questions will engender vague
  answers.  :-)

  More complex devices -- such as RAID controllers -- may require
  device-specific configuration steps.  (And -- obviously -- if you
  cannot tell us which widgets, we can only provide vague answers...)

:  I'm noe even familiar with VMS, so maybe I'm getting myself
:into a real mess.

  Get the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) -- this will get
  you pointers to many available resources, and will answer many common
  questions: ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms

  If this is a "rush job", you may want to obtain some help.  (This
  job is certainly not difficult -- the variations and possibilities
  are just rather hard to describe in a news posting such as this.)

