Yes, i did. I'm using DU4.0B on my Multia. I think you nedd at least 1G of
hdd, and 32m of memory to run this beast.
To install DU, you nedd to switch to the SRM console. At the ARC(blue)
console find the 'Switch to the DIgital Unix console' menu, and follow the
instruction. Then power cycle the machine to get the ARC(black) >>> console.
I assume that you have a SCSI cd attached to the machinme and the DU install
CD.
At the ARC console you can issue various command. You can list drives
attached to your system: sho device (IMHO). Find your cd drive as dka.....
Then try to boot the CD issuing the: boot dka....( the correct device name
here).
When the CD booted up, follow the installation instruction.

Mihaly



