Did you happen to install the instruction sheet under the tape when you
put it in the drive? I've seen this happen several times, and the only
solution is to pull it out (needle nose pliers a must).

If there isn't this, you may want to try powering down the drive
to reset it's confusion.

You should really try to determine the cause of the lockup and
fix it.

The last possible step is to release the door lock (there's a selonoid
on the side of the drive that you can move by hand tht will let the
door open even though it is loaded. You can then pull out the tape, but
you will have to reset the hook inside of the tape drive to it's normal
unloaded position (Which can be a real pain)

I'm assuming it IS a TK50, and not a TZ30 you're talking about.
A TZ30 is much harder to straighten out, but it fails less often.




