In article <511890954wnr@natron.demon.co.uk>,
Roger Barnett  <Roger@natron.demon.co.uk> wrote:
>
>Ok, I'm sure I've done this in the distant past but...
>
>
>is there a way of getting a stuck TK50 tape out of the drive ?
>

  Yes, but it's painful...  Here's what I did.
  Take the tape drive out of its chassis following all the usual percautions
(take care with cables and so on.) Remove the big metal cover from the back of
the drive; this will expose the inner reel where the tape lives.  There is a
solenoid on the left of the drive (with the front towards you) that locks the
handle down.  If you can get the tape off the inner reel you should be able to
pull the solenoid's "arm" and release the tape cartridge.
  Now all you have to do is put the leader back on.  :-)  It's actually not too
bad as long as you're careful with it.
  Good luck.

