Niclas Mattsson <niclas@entek.chalmers.se> writes:
>I'm trying to figure out a suitable configuration for a new Personal
>Workstation. My main application is nonlinear optimization with very
>large problem sizes. The question is: will the extra 2 MB cache help me?
>[...]

Probably not.  On older machine big caches were essential, but my
experience on a PWS 500 is:

  * problems with small working sets (a few megs) speed up but not a
    whole lot because the main SDRAM is so fast.
  * big problems (tens of megs and up) will usually be *slowed down*
    since the cache kills bandwidth.

If you need to run big problems, instead of spending $xxx on cache
spend it on on souping up other aspects of the machine.

Disclaimers: YMMV, IMHO etc.

