On Tue, 09 Sep 1997 15:27:58 GMT, dave@jhgate.carenet.org (David
Stephens) wrote:

>
>Subject line says it...
>
>I inherited a tower with 2 RZ74 drives, now I want to move them to a
>different system. I don't see any external switches for changing the
>SCSI ID, and of course I _didn't_ inherit the dox.
>
>Help?

This is from memory, so bear with me.

On the jumper block, you will see something like this:

:::.::::::
       421

Note that there is one jumper with a pin missing.  There are more
jumpers on ones side of this pin than the other.  In my example,
it is the right side.  I've labeled them as Id's 4,2,1.  Jumping
these in different combinations will get you Id's 1-7 (0=no
jumper).

This may be upside down and/or backwards, but just go to the far
side of the half with more jumpers after the 'broken' jumper.

Try it and let me know if it doesn't work.  I'll look at mine for
a solid example if this isn't working for you.




