Just a quick review,

1. During the installation process, you are asked if you have any other
disk controllers to look for, and it is at this point that you have the
option of loading the Windows NT V4.0 driver for the Adpatec. You insert
the floppy disk and off you go, right?

Part pf your problem would probably be related to having to define a
SystemPartition. This should be a small, 5 to 10MB partition at the end of
the disk drive that is where the HAL, PAL and OSLOADER will be stored.
This requirement is for our friends at Microsoft who created the ARC
Console, now frontended with ALphaBIOS, and ARC does not understand NTFS,
only FAT. This preperation of the disk must be done before you start the
install, so in fact, it does look like you have a catch 22 here.

