Michael Storie wrote:
> 
> I'm looking for information on setting up hardware devices like RAID
> and print etc on a DEC Alpha running VMS.  Does anyone know where I
> can obtain either online or downloadable system configuration
> information this?  I'm sorry that I can't be more specific about
> hardware being used etc.., but I don't have that information in front
> of me.  I'm noe even familiar with VMS, so maybe I'm getting myself
> into a real mess.

What do you mean by "setting up"?  If you are connecting devices to
a VMS machine that are supported by that version of VMS, then you 
can use system management utilities to configure them.

For oVMS/AXP (no actual experience on my part here, just looking
at the manuals) you should configure hardware connected to your
system by:

$ RUN SYS$SYSTEM:SYSMAN
SYSMAN> IO AUTOCONFIGURE

This should connect the devices and load their drivers.  For more
information see the "OpenVMS System Manager's Manual: Essentials" 
and the "OpenVMS System Management Utilities Reference Manual" in 
the oVMS documentation set.  (If you don't have a doc set, at 
least get the basic set and the system management set)
