OpenVMS has a huge (sorry HUGE) documentation set that comes with it. If
you read every manual from cover to cover at least twice (I have), you
will have at your disposal instant and gratifying knowledge about almost
all aspects of OpenVMS. The manuals you want are, the System Managers
Guide, and Guide to Setting Up and OpenVMS system, and the Installation
Guide for OpenVMS. Ok, maybe I can't remember the exact titles, we've
changed them a few times over the years.

For your RAID setup, you must specifically refer to the RAID configuration
guide that came with that option. Hardware RAID setup is not within the
bounds of OpenVMS.

If this is a product like the SWXCR, then there should be at least 4
manulas kicking around for that, one for UNIX, one for NT and one for
OpenVMS and finally a manual for the SWXCR utilities.

