>The 11/02 was a half size (but just as capable as) the 11/03.  The Falcon
>was a single chip only sold as a controller (well, maybe they put it on a
>Q-BUS).  The 11/23 was the new LSI-11 chip set, and the 11/24 was the
>Unibus version.  No personal experience on the rest....

You're confusing systems, boards and chipsets.  As far as I'm aware, there
was no pdp11/02.  What there was was the LSI-11 chipset, which came on the
quad-wide LSI-11 card, and the dual wide LSI-11/2 card.  Same chipset, same
architecture, but some of the LSI-11 models had onboard memory.  Both cards
found their way into pdp11/03 systems.

The F-11 chipset is found on the LSI-11/23 card, which is found in pdp11/23
systems.  The F-11 is also used on the CPU cards of the pdp11/24, and the 
pdp11/23+.

-- don



