I wonder how many Bridgeport Series I CNC vertical mills are still running in
machine shops out there? We shipped thousands of these in the late 70's- early
80's with an LSI-11 running the show. OS in 4KW ROM and another 4KW of onboard
RAM that was shared part program store and system/stack space. 3 axis linear
and 2 axis circular interpolation was done in software, one .0005" step ahead,
and hardware registers were INC/DEC'd in an ISR for the "line time clock" which
was really a ramped VCO peaking at 20khz or so. Our clock board also had a
cycle stealing DRAM refresh so we could disable the CPU board DRAM refresh. It
ran in burst mode and preempted the clock interrupt, making the axis step
motors misstep.

