> Our Analytical Chemistry Laboratory has an ICP mass spec (a big
> expensive instrument to non-chemists like me) controlled by a Falcon. 
> The Falcon, also called an SBC-11/21 if my memory serves me correctly,
> is a dual size board containing a T11 unmapped PDP-11 on a chip, 16KW
> of RAM, a pair of serial interfaces, and a parallel interface.  The
> parallel interface goes to to the instrument's control circuitry and
> one of the serial interfaces goes to an LSI-11/73.
> 
> The LSI-11/73 originally ran RSX-11M/Plus booted from an RL02, but now
> has a SCSI disk on a CMD host adaptor.  It talks to the Falcon using
> direct QIOs to Jim McGlinchey's DZV driver.  The RSX terminal driver
> keeps up with the DZV most of the time, but the instrument's
> communication protocol doesn't recover from lost interrupts, which
> loses measurements.  We switched to Jim McGlinchey's driver, and it
> has never lost an interrupt.
