I'm pretty sure that the 11/05 and 11/10 that I have have 4-level interrupts.
In fact, I _know_ the 4 BR lines go to different places in the CPU logic, 
as I had to work through that circuitry while tracing a CPU fault.


But I believe that some model numbers were used for machines _other than_
the ones they were originally intended for. Remember that the 11/05 came out
quite late - after the 11/45, for example. The initial table of machines in
`Computer Engineering' is rather different to the machines that actually
appeared. 

I can't comment on the 11/15 and 11/20, though. 


: Tim.

