In article <MPG.e7631437725a171989686@news.pnm.net>,
Christian J. Bauer <christian.bauer@passau.netsurf.de> wrote:

>It has TWO power connection! The system manual describes the second as 
>being used for the 3.3V PCI Slots. Never saw that on a PC board.
>Are there any Power Supplies out there with TWO power connectors?

Yes, there are such PSUs available. I had to look through a dozen
or so cases before I found one that also had a 3.3V power supply.
If you really want one, check out cases that have PS/2 keyboard/mouse
connector holes. (Not that the holes are the same width as the
AXPpci33 in most cases.)

However, there's no need at all for the 3.3V supply unless you have
a PCI card that needs 3.3V. (The CPU has its own voltage regulator.)
I've never seen such a PCI card. I've got an AXPpci33 running on
just 5/12V, and it works fine.

BTW, make sure you have a fan low in the front of the case blowing
directly through the CPU heatsink and voltage regulator.

(This was both e-mailed and posted.)

