Use the BNC connector for what?  You can plug it into a TV monitor but that
connection is not meant for terminal communications.

If you look at the back of the terminal, you'll find a 25pin D, a 20 ma loop
and the BNC.  On the label next to the back, you should see the letters COMM
next to the D connector.  There is a "monitor screen" ICON next to the BNC.
You select the COMM (EIA or 20 ma) from the setup screen.

> Also I need to know if they are compatible with NetWare 3.1x server and/or
> NT 4.0? I would like to use them as demos in my classroom so if anyone can
> help it would be greatly appreciated.

Why not?  If you can connect the terminals to a suitable serial I/O connect-
ion and the application outputs ascii, the terminal should work fine.

