In article <MPG.e7631437725a171989686@news.pnm.net>,
Christian J. Bauer <christian.bauer@passau.netsurf.de> wrote:
>I bought a AXPpci33 (UDB) board and am confused about the power 
>connections.
>
>It has TWO power connection! The system manual describes the second as 
>being used for the 3.3V PCI Slots. Never saw that on a PC board.
>
>Are there any Power Supplies out there with TWO power connectors?

The AXPpci33 manual lists some power supply made by Intel I think, but
don't worry about it because the 3.3V PCI power supply is not necessary if
you'll be using standard PC peripherals, which still run on 5V, so you can
use a normal power supply and leave the 3.3V connectors alone.  The 3.3V
for the CPU is derived from the usual 5V using a voltage regulator next
to the CPU (which gets hot by the way, point a fan at it if you can).

